# Global production invariants

These should become non-negotiable acceptance criteria across all sprints.

## Invariant 1: no publish without fresh validation

Before any import or export:

```text
read fresh Core snapshot
read fresh Google mirror/live state
compare pinned hashes
validate field capability
validate field policy
validate section execution plan
reject stale decisions
```

## Invariant 2: field-level UI, section-level execution

The UI can allow field-level decisions, but execution must group them into Google-safe resource operations.

Example:

```text
User selected:
- export Monday hours
- export Tuesday hours
- export Friday hours

Backend executes:
- one regularHours publish plan
- one Google updateMask
- one section-level validation
- child audit rows for selected fields
```

## Invariant 3: every field has policy

No syncable field should exist without:

```text
field_key
section_key
importable
exportable
authority policy
semantic comparator
risk level
write group
Google update strategy
rollback/retry behavior
```

## Invariant 4: every external write is auditable

Every Google/Core write should store:

```text
actor
timestamp
decision payload
pinned hashes
before hashes
after hashes
write group
Google updateMask / attributeMask
request summary
response summary
error code
retry metadata
final recompute result
```

The existing `dual_sync_publish_operations` table is the correct foundation for this. 

## Invariant 5: every production failure has a clear operator state

No generic “sync failed” for production. The system should classify failures as:

```text
reauth_required
location_access_lost
quota_limited
google_validation_failed
stale_decision
unsupported_field
permission_denied
external_api_error
core_write_failed
partial_publish_failed
```

