# Sprint 2 — Transactional sync execution and locking

**Goal:** Make refresh and publish safe under concurrency.

The architecture already has manual refresh, snapshot runs, state recomputation, publish orchestration, pinned hashes, operation rows, candidate resolution, and final recompute.  This sprint makes them behave as one production transaction boundary.

## Backend stories

### DS-201 — Add per-restaurant/provider lock

Implement a lock around:

```text
refreshFromGoogle
runPublish
scheduled refresh
core_write-triggered recompute
location linking initial sync
```

Lock key:

```text
restaurant_id + provider
```

Lock behavior:

```text
acquire lock
reject or queue concurrent publish
allow read-only state fetch
release lock on success/failure
expire abandoned locks
record lock holder and job id
```

Possible storage:

```text
dual_sync_locks
or PostgreSQL advisory locks
or queue-level uniqueness
```

### DS-202 — Add publish job idempotency

Every publish request gets:

```text
client_request_id
publish_batch_id
actor_user_id
restaurant_id
provider
decision_hash
```

Duplicate submit should not double-write.

### DS-203 — Add pinned snapshot validation as hard gate

Before execution:

```text
compare pinnedCoreSnapshotHash
compare pinnedGbpSnapshotHash
compare per-field pinned hashes
reject stale decisions
return stale fields to UI
```

### DS-204 — Convert publish loop to transaction phases

Recommended phases:

```text
PHASE 1: validate
PHASE 2: plan
PHASE 3: preflight
PHASE 4: execute
PHASE 5: refresh affected mirrors
PHASE 6: recompute
PHASE 7: finalize audit
```

Important: do not hold a database transaction open while calling Google. Use a logical transaction/job with operation state records.

### DS-205 — Add operation group model

The codemap records one operation per field.  Keep that, but add a parent group for section-level execution.

Suggested table:

```sql
dual_sync_publish_batches
dual_sync_publish_operation_groups
dual_sync_publish_operations
```

Group example:

```text
Batch #123
  Group #A: export regularHours
    Operation: operatingHours.monday
    Operation: operatingHours.tuesday
    Operation: operatingHours.friday
```

## QA stories

### DS-206 — Concurrency test suite

Simulate:

```text
two admins publish same field
admin publishes while refresh is running
core write arrives during publish
scheduled refresh overlaps manual refresh
Google changes after user review but before publish
retry of same publish request
browser double-click publish
```

## Acceptance criteria

```text
Only one write-affecting sync job runs per restaurant/provider
Duplicate publish request does not create duplicate Google writes
Stale decisions are rejected before mutation
Refresh/publish overlap cannot corrupt field state
Partial failure is recorded at group and field level
Final recompute always runs unless the job never reaches execution
```

