# Sprint 5 — Queue, retry, and outbound candidate system

**Goal:** Turn outbound candidates into a production-grade sync queue.

The codemap already includes `dual_sync_outbound_candidates`, with one open candidate per restaurant/provider/field, and publish operations resolve candidates after export.  This sprint hardens that into a reliable queue/outbox pattern.

## Backend stories

### DS-501 — Add sync job queue

Job types:

```text
google_refresh_manual
google_refresh_scheduled
google_refresh_location_link
core_write_recompute
publish_import
publish_export
publish_batch
reauth_check
mirror_refresh_after_publish
```

Each job:

```text
restaurant_id
provider
job_kind
priority
idempotency_key
status
attempt_count
next_run_at
locked_by
error_code
error_payload
```

### DS-502 — Debounce Core writes

When Core changes rapidly:

```text
update hours
update phone
update website
update menu
```

Do not immediately create multiple Google writes. Instead:

```text
collect outbound candidates
debounce per restaurant/provider
recompute once
create one publish recommendation batch
```

### DS-503 — Strengthen outbound candidate lifecycle

Current lifecycle:

```text
open -> resolved/superseded/cancelled
```

Add richer states:

```text
open
blocked_conflict
pending_publish
resolved
superseded
cancelled
failed
expired
```

### DS-504 — Candidate supersession rules

If Core changes the same field again:

```text
old open candidate -> superseded
new candidate -> open
baseline_google_hash preserved
new proposed_value stored
```

### DS-505 — Retry and dead-letter handling

Retry only safe failures:

```text
network timeout
quota limited
temporary 5xx
```

Do not retry automatically:

```text
validation failure
unsupported field
permission denied
reauth required
stale decision
```

Dead-letter after threshold:

```text
max_attempts = 3 or 5
requires operator/admin review
```

