# Final recommendation

Use this as a **production hardening roadmap**, not a rewrite roadmap.

The architecture should remain:

```text
OAuth + location link
Google mirror tables
canonical snapshots
dynamic registry
field states
outbound candidates
publish operations
final recompute
```

The sprint plan should strengthen it into:

```text
policy-driven registry
semantic state engine
locked sync transaction model
section-level publish planner
safe Google adapters
queued/idempotent execution
operator-grade UX
fake-Google/replay testing
observable rollout
```

The most important engineering milestone is **Sprint 3 + Sprint 4 together**: once field decisions are converted into safe section-level publish plans and every Google write has explicit mask/preflight/quota/error behavior, the architecture becomes much closer to production-safe.

